          "text": "A post–Pending Close event was recorded for work order **WO-2025-09-004** (**MO-25-09-1070**, Cooler Plate Pack) at Modine’s Racine site.\n\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070` (event `CE-250904-0004`, INPUT/component issue)\n- **Amount:** **$284,763.42** (28,476,342 cents)\n- **Event created:** `2025-09-30T19:15:00`\n- **September Pending Close time:** `2025-09-30T18:00:00`\n- **How late:** **75 minutes**\n- **Recorded accounting status:** **POSTED**\n- **Status consistent with Oracle policy? No.** Oracle’s supplied policy says new transactions falling in or before a period in Pending Close won’t be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting. This INPUT event is not among the listed exceptions, so its recorded POSTED status is inconsistent with that treatment.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed. The report was submitted, and its current receipt state is `needs_evidence`.",
